    {
      "name": "00 Monitor Factory",
      "description": "# AIEI Monitor Factory\n\n## The Story\n\nManual measurement doesn't scale. The Monitor Factory is the automation layer that turns AIEI from a one-time assessment into a continuous measurement system.\n\nIt creates Postman monitors for each scoring collection, configures schedules (hourly, daily, weekly), sets up notification channels, and manages the lifecycle of running monitors. This is the bridge between Level 2 (Reactive) and Level 3 (Defined) on the maturity model — the point where measurement becomes systematic rather than ad hoc.\n\nThe factory approach means you don't configure monitors one at a time. You describe what you want monitored and how often, and the factory provisions everything. It also handles the operational reality of monitors: checking status, reviewing run history, and cleaning up monitors that are no longer needed.\n\n## The Pipeline\n\n### 1. List Workspace Collections\nDiscovers all AIEI collections in the workspace that are eligible for monitoring.\n\n### 2. List Existing Monitors\nChecks what's already being monitored to avoid duplication.\n\n### 3. Create Scoring Monitors\nProvisions monitors for the scoring pipeline collections with appropriate schedules and the AIEI Configuration environment.\n\n### 4. Verify Monitor Status\nConfirms all monitors are running and healthy.\n\n### 5. Review Run History\nPulls recent monitor execution results to verify the pipeline is producing valid scores.\n\n## What Comes Next\n→ [17 AIEI Cloud Audit](collection/20784047-c476d1a4-c92f-40c4-94c9-b256e1caf726) to audit your Postman workspace configuration\n→ [22 AIEI Orchestration](collection/20784047-6177ecf0-ac19-43a4-a5ca-69beaafafb2b) for enterprise-grade pipeline management",
      "item": [
