    {
      "name": "01 Benchmark Validation",
      "description": "# AIEI Benchmark Validation\n\n## The Story\n\nYour AIEI score means nothing in isolation. Is 0.72 good? Bad? Average? The Benchmark Validation collection answers this by comparing your scores against industry benchmarks, DORA metrics, and peer cohorts.\n\nBenchmarking serves two purposes. First, it calibrates expectations — a Composite Score of 0.65 might be excellent for an organization that started AI adoption three months ago. Second, it detects scoring anomalies — if your R-Score is 0.95 but the industry median is 0.70, either you're genuinely exceptional or your measurement has a bias.\n\nThe collection validates each dimension independently and flags scores that are statistical outliers (more than 2 standard deviations from the benchmark mean). Outliers aren't necessarily wrong, but they deserve investigation.\n\n## The Pipeline\n\n### 1. Fetch Industry Benchmarks\nRetrieves benchmark data including industry medians, percentile distributions, and DORA reference metrics.\n\n### 2. Validate Scores Against Benchmarks\nCompares your scores to benchmarks, computes percentile rankings, and flags statistical outliers.\n\n### 3. Generate Validation Report\nProduces a calibrated view of your scores with benchmark context, percentile rankings, and outlier explanations.\n\n## What Comes Next\n→ [19 AIEI Falsifiability Watchdog](collection/20784047-4cbb5515-821c-431c-9704-53986ceb72d1) to stress-test your scores\n→ [09 AIEI Executive Report](collection/20784047-f3dae730-c7fc-4796-a387-a95361326551) to include benchmark context in executive briefings",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Validate R Formula",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "",
                  "// Compute R-Score from mock reference data",
                  "",
                  "const cfr_ai = res.cfr_ai;",
                  "",
                  "const slo_attainment = res.slo_attainment;",
                  "",
                  "const contract_catch_rate = res.contract_catch_rate;",
                  "",
                  "const uptime_ai = res.uptime_ai;",
                  "",
                  "const adaptability = res.adaptability;",
                  "",
                  "",
                  "const R = (1 - cfr_ai) * slo_attainment * contract_catch_rate * uptime_ai",
                  "* adaptability;",
                  "",
                  "",
                  "console.log(`R-Score computed: ${R.toFixed(4)}`);",
                  "",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"R formula: expected ~0.6962 MODERATE\", function () {",
                  "    // Assert R is approximately 0.6962 within tolerance",
                  "    pm.expect(Math.abs(R - 0.6962)).to.be.below(0.001,",
                  "        `R=${R.toFixed(4)} is not within 0.001 of expected 0.6962`);",
                  "",
                  "    // Assert classification is MODERATE (R > 0.50 and R <= 0.70)",
                  "    const classification = R > 0.70 ? \"STRONG\" :",
                  "                           R > 0.50 ? \"MODERATE\" : \"FRAGILE\";",
                  "    pm.expect(classification).to.eql(\"MODERATE\",",
                  "        `Expected MODERATE but got ${classification} for R=${R.toFixed(4)}`);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{mock_base_url}}/stub/cfr",
              "host": [
                "{{mock_base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "stub",
                "cfr"
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Validate Q Formula",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "",
                  "// Compute Q-Score from mock reference data",
                  "",
                  "const defect_component = 1 - (res.defect_rate_ai / res.defect_rate_nonai);",
                  "",
                  "const test_pass_rate_delta = Math.min(res.ai_test_pass_rate /",
                  "res.manual_test_pass_rate, 1.0);",
                  "",
                  "const Q = defect_component * test_pass_rate_delta * (1 -",
                  "res.rework_rate_ai);",
                  "",
                  "",
                  "console.log(`Q-Score computed: ${Q.toFixed(4)}`);",
                  "",
                  "console.log(`  defect_component: ${defect_component.toFixed(4)}`);",
                  "",
                  "console.log(`  test_pass_rate_delta: ${test_pass_rate_delta.toFixed(4)}`);",
                  "",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Q formula: expected ~0.2483 TECHNICAL DEBT\", function () {",
                  "    // Assert Q is approximately 0.2483 within tolerance",
                  "    pm.expect(Math.abs(Q - 0.2483)).to.be.below(0.001,",
                  "        `Q=${Q.toFixed(4)} is not within 0.001 of expected 0.2483`);",
                  "",
                  "    // Assert classification is TECHNICAL DEBT (Q < 0.50)",
                  "    const classification = Q >= 0.70 ? \"STRONG\" :",
                  "                           Q >= 0.50 ? \"MODERATE\" : \"TECHNICAL DEBT\";",
                  "    pm.expect(classification).to.eql(\"TECHNICAL DEBT\",",
                  "        `Expected TECHNICAL DEBT but got ${classification} for Q=${Q.toFixed(4)}`);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{mock_base_url}}/stub/defect-rates",
              "host": [
                "{{mock_base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "stub",
