    {
      "name": "03 Orchestration",
      "description": "# AIEI Orchestration Layer\n\nRun the AIEI Scoring Pipeline without depending on Postman Monitors. This collection wires MCP and CI/CD orchestration options so partners and engineers can trigger pipeline execution from GitHub Actions, CircleCI, n8n, or Temporal.\n\n## Options (in order of primacy)\n\n1. **Newman MCP Runner** - Use `shannonlal/mcp-postman` to run collections via MCP. Agent Mode or any MCP client can invoke run-collection.\n2. **GitHub Actions Dispatch** - Trigger a GitHub Action that runs Newman. Primary CI path.\n3. **CircleCI Pipeline Trigger** - Trigger a CircleCI pipeline that runs the AIEI pipeline. Backup to GitHub.\n4. **n8n Webhook** - Send a webhook to an n8n workflow that runs Newman, checks results, posts to Slack.\n5. **Temporal Workflow** - Start a Temporal workflow that runs the pipeline as a durable Activity with retries.\n6. **Orchestration Status** - Visualizer showing which backends are configured and the recommended path.\n\nThis collection is in the Developer Kit only (not Executive). Orchestration config is an engineering concern.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Newman MCP Runner",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.environment.set('orchestration_newman_mcp_note', 'Install: npx -y @smithery/cli install mcp-postman --client claude. Tool: run-collection.');",
                  "pm.environment.set('orchestration_newman_available', 'true');",
                  "const html = '<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><style>body{font-family:system-ui;background:#212121;color:#e0e0e0;padding:24px}.card{background:#3D2E6B;border:1px solid #3D2E6B;border-radius:12px;padding:16px;margin:12px 0}.k{font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#757575}.v{font-size:18px;margin-top:6px;color:#FF6C37}</style></head><body><div class=\"card\"><div class=\"k\">Newman MCP</div><div class=\"v\">shannonlal/mcp-postman - run-collection tool</div><div style=\"font-size:12px;color:#9E9E9E;margin-top:8px\">Install: npx -y @smithery/cli install mcp-postman --client claude</div></div></body></html>';",
                  "pm.visualizer.set(html);",
                  "pm.test('Newman MCP documented', function() { pm.expect(true).to.be.true; });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{mock_base_url}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{mock_base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Run the AIEI pipeline via Newman wrapped as an MCP tool.\n\n**Setup:** Install the community MCP server `shannonlal/mcp-postman`:\n- `npx -y @smithery/cli install mcp-postman --client claude`\n- Or clone https://github.com/shannonlal/mcp-postman and run locally\n\nThe server exposes a `run-collection` tool that accepts collection URL/path, environment file, and iteration count. Returns pass/fail, timing, failure details.\n\nThis request checks if Newman is available locally and stores a flag for the Orchestration Status Dashboard."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. GitHub Actions Dispatch",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const ref = pm.environment.get('github_workflow_ref') || 'main';",
                  "if (pm.request.body && pm.request.body.raw) {",
                  "  try {",
                  "    const b = JSON.parse(pm.request.body.raw);",
                  "    b.ref = ref;",
                  "    pm.request.body.raw = JSON.stringify(b);",
                  "  } catch (e) {}",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const code = pm.response.code;",
                  "const configured = (pm.environment.get('github_token') || '').trim() && (pm.environment.get('github_owner') || '').trim() && (pm.environment.get('github_repo') || '').trim();",
                  "pm.environment.set('orchestration_github_configured', configured ? 'true' : 'false');",
                  "pm.environment.set('orchestration_github_last_status', String(code));",
                  "if (code === 204) {",
                  "  console.log('GitHub Actions workflow dispatched. Check Actions tab for run.');",
                  "} else if (code === 404) {",
                  "  console.log('Workflow not found. Set github_workflow_id to the workflow filename or numeric ID.');",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('GitHub dispatch attempted', function() { pm.expect([204, 404, 401, 403]).to.include(code); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{github_token}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/vnd.github+json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-GitHub-Api-Version",
                "value": "2022-11-28"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://api.github.com/repos/{{github_owner}}/{{github_repo}}/actions/workflows/{{github_workflow_id}}/dispatches",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "api",
                "github",
                "com"
              ],
              "path": [
                "repos",
                "{{github_owner}}",
                "{{github_repo}}",
                "actions",
                "workflows",
                "{{github_workflow_id}}",
                "dispatches"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Trigger a GitHub Actions workflow that runs the AIEI Scoring Pipeline via Newman.\n\n**Prerequisites:** Set github_token, github_owner, github_repo, github_workflow_id (filename or numeric ID). The workflow must exist and call Newman with the AIEI collection + environment.\n\nThis is the primary CI path for pipeline execution without Postman Monitors."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3. CircleCI Pipeline Trigger",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const code = pm.response.code;",
                  "const configured = (pm.environment.get('circleci_token') || '').trim() && (pm.environment.get('circleci_project_slug') || '').trim();",
                  "pm.environment.set('orchestration_circleci_configured', configured ? 'true' : 'false');",
                  "pm.environment.set('orchestration_circleci_last_status', String(code));",
                  "if (code === 201) {",
                  "  const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (data.number) console.log('CircleCI pipeline #' + data.number + ' created.');",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('CircleCI trigger attempted', function() { pm.expect([201, 400, 401, 404]).to.include(code); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Circle-Token",
                "value": "{{circleci_token}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://circleci.com/api/v2/project/{{circleci_project_slug}}/pipeline",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "circleci",
                "com"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v2",
                "project",
                "{{circleci_project_slug}}",
                "pipeline"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Trigger a CircleCI pipeline that runs the AIEI Scoring Pipeline. Backup to GitHub Actions.\n\n**Prerequisites:** Set circleci_token (API token), circleci_project_slug (e.g. gh/owner/repo). The pipeline config must include a job that runs Newman with the AIEI collection."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "4. n8n Webhook Trigger",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.request.body && pm.request.body.raw) {",
                  "  try {",
                  "    const b = JSON.parse(pm.request.body.raw);",
                  "    b.ts = new Date().toISOString();",
                  "    pm.request.body.raw = JSON.stringify(b);",
                  "  } catch (e) {}",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const configured = (pm.environment.get('n8n_webhook_url') || '').trim().length > 0;",
                  "pm.environment.set('orchestration_n8n_configured', configured ? 'true' : 'false');",
                  "pm.environment.set('orchestration_n8n_last_status', String(pm.response.code));",
                  "pm.test('n8n webhook attempted', function() { pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.within(200, 499); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{n8n_webhook_url}}/",
              "host": [
                "{{n8n_webhook_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                ""
              ]
            },
            "description": "Send a webhook to an n8n workflow that runs the AIEI pipeline.\n\n**Flow:** n8n receives this POST, runs Newman (or calls MCP), checks results, posts summary to Slack, optionally creates a ticket. Set n8n_webhook_url to your workflow webhook URL.\n\n**Prerequisites:** n8n_webhook_url must be set. The n8n workflow should: run Newman with AIEI collection + env, parse output, push to Slack, and optionally create Jira/Linear ticket."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Temporal Workflow Trigger",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const configured = (pm.environment.get('temporal_endpoint') || '').trim().length > 0;",
                  "pm.environment.set('orchestration_temporal_configured', configured ? 'true' : 'false');",
                  "pm.environment.set('orchestration_temporal_last_status', String(pm.response.code));",
                  "pm.test('Temporal trigger attempted', function() { pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.within(200, 499); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{temporal_endpoint}}/",
              "host": [
                "{{temporal_endpoint}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                ""
              ]
            },
            "description": "Start a Temporal workflow that runs the AIEI pipeline as a durable Activity with retries.\n\n**Architecture:** Wrap the AIEI Scoring Pipeline (Newman run) as a Temporal Activity. This request calls Temporal's HTTP API (or a proxy) to start the workflow. The workflow runs the pipeline, handles retries, and can signal completion to other workflows.\n\n**Prerequisites:** Set temporal_endpoint to your Temporal frontend HTTP endpoint or a small proxy that starts the workflow (e.g. Temporal Webhook or custom adapter). Workflow ID and Task Queue should be configured in your Temporal setup."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Orchestration Status Dashboard",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const gh = (pm.environment.get('orchestration_github_configured') || 'false') === 'true';",
                  "const circle = (pm.environment.get('orchestration_circleci_configured') || 'false') === 'true';",
                  "const n8n = (pm.environment.get('n8n_webhook_url') || '').trim().length > 0;",
                  "const temporal = (pm.environment.get('temporal_endpoint') || '').trim().length > 0;",
                  "const newman = (pm.environment.get('orchestration_newman_available') || 'false') === 'true';",
                  "const options = [",
                  "  { name: 'Newman MCP', ok: newman, rec: true },",
                  "  { name: 'GitHub Actions', ok: gh, rec: !newman && gh },",
                  "  { name: 'CircleCI', ok: circle, rec: !newman && !gh && circle },",
                  "  { name: 'n8n Webhook', ok: n8n, rec: !newman && !gh && !circle && n8n },",
                  "  { name: 'Temporal', ok: temporal, rec: !newman && !gh && !circle && !n8n && temporal }",
                  "];",
                  "let rec = options.find(o => o.rec) || options.find(o => o.ok) || options[0];",
                  "const rows = options.map(o => '<tr><td>' + o.name + '</td><td style=\"color:' + (o.ok ? '#FF6C37' : '#6B4FBB') + '\">' + (o.ok ? 'Configured' : 'Not set') + '</td><td>' + (o === rec ? 'Recommended' : '') + '</td></tr>').join('');",
                  "const html = '<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><style>body{font-family:system-ui;background:#212121;color:#e0e0e0;padding:24px}h2{color:#fff;font-size:18px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}.card{background:#3D2E6B;border:1px solid #3D2E6B;border-radius:12px;padding:16px;margin:12px 0}td{padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #3D2E6B}.rec{color:#FF6C37;font-weight:600}</style></head><body><div class=\"card\"><h2>Orchestration status</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Path</th><th>Status</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody>' + rows + '</tbody></table><p style=\"margin-top:16px;font-size:12px;color:#9E9E9E\">Recommended path: ' + rec.name + '. Set env vars and run requests 1-5 to refresh.</p></div></body></html>';",
                  "pm.visualizer.set(html);",
                  "pm.test('Status dashboard rendered', function() { pm.expect(true).to.be.true; });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{mock_base_url}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{mock_base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Visualizer showing which orchestration paths are configured (from env) and the recommended path.\n\nRun after configuring env vars and/or running requests 1-5. Green = configured/available, amber = not configured."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}